// Helper for #1320. Contributes ONE diagnostic, of a different code and from a
// different file than b-side.cnx, so the entry asserts two DISTINCT diagnostics
// rather than the same one reported twice.

u32 declaredHere() {
    return 3;
}

// Control, must stay SILENT: `declaredHere` is declared in this very file, so a
// value reference to it is defined, which is all E0427 asks. Without this, an
// analyzer that rejected every function-as-value would still pass the
// assertion below. It takes the function-body form because that is the
// spelling that also compiles (ADR-029, and #1497/#1498 for the file-scope
// form).
u32 useLocal() {
    declaredHere ownRef <- declaredHere;
    return ownRef();
}

// The defect this half contributes: declared in no file at all.
u32 fromNowhere <- neverDeclaredInA;
